  note: the other group names `fixedbugs-563-tcl.h` at line 12
  note: C keeps a macro as it is defined until it is undone, and refuses a definition that disagrees (C11 6.10.3p2), so the order of the two decides what a line reading `FIXEDBUGS_563_EXTERN` means: read as this unit reads them, `fixedbugs-563-tcl.h` first, its own lines would read `FIXEDBUGS_563_EXTERN` as `fixedbugs-563-tcl.h` line 1 defines it and every line after `fixedbugs-563-jpeg.h` line 1 as that line defines it
